
NETWORK 18 "Commanded Plant Timeline"
  COMMENT "Each commanded signal is a two-edge timeline and nothing more: it holds its initial level until Edge1, takes the opposite level from Edge1 until Edge2, and returns to its initial level at Edge2. Both edge times are measured from the start of the scenario, so a timeline says nothing about the cleardowns on either side of it. Setting Edge1 equal to Edge2 is how a timeline says the signal never changes - it collapses to the initial level for the whole scenario, whichever level that is - and setting both at or past the scenario end says the same thing with the change scheduled after everything has finished. One shape per signal, written once and identically ten times, so a reader who has understood one rung has understood the network."
  COIL TlHopper := (ScenT < Stim.HopperEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.HopperEdge2) AND Stim.HopperInitial OR NOT Stim.HopperInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.HopperEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.HopperEdge2
  COIL TlManualCycle := (ScenT < Stim.ManualCycleEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.ManualCycleEdge2) AND Stim.ManualCycleInitial OR NOT Stim.ManualCycleInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.ManualCycleEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.ManualCycleEdge2
  COIL TlJogExtend := (ScenT < Stim.JogExtendEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.JogExtendEdge2) AND Stim.JogExtendInitial OR NOT Stim.JogExtendInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.JogExtendEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.JogExtendEdge2
  COIL TlJogRetract := (ScenT < Stim.JogRetractEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.JogRetractEdge2) AND Stim.JogRetractInitial OR NOT Stim.JogRetractInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.JogRetractEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.JogRetractEdge2
  COIL TlHome := (ScenT < Stim.HomeEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.HomeEdge2) AND Stim.HomeInitial OR NOT Stim.HomeInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.HomeEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.HomeEdge2
  COIL TlFullTravel := (ScenT < Stim.FullTravelEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.FullTravelEdge2) AND Stim.FullTravelInitial OR NOT Stim.FullTravelInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.FullTravelEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.FullTravelEdge2
  COIL TlHighPressure := (ScenT < Stim.HighPressureEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.HighPressureEdge2) AND Stim.HighPressureInitial OR NOT Stim.HighPressureInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.HighPressureEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.HighPressureEdge2
  COIL TlPackRunning := (ScenT < Stim.PackRunningEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.PackRunningEdge2) AND Stim.PackRunningInitial OR NOT Stim.PackRunningInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.PackRunningEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.PackRunningEdge2
  COIL TlHealthy := (ScenT < Stim.HealthyEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.HealthyEdge2) AND Stim.HealthyInitial OR NOT Stim.HealthyInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.HealthyEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.HealthyEdge2
  COIL TlDownstream := (ScenT < Stim.DownstreamEdge1 OR ScenT >= Stim.DownstreamEdge2) AND Stim.DownstreamInitial OR NOT Stim.DownstreamInitial AND ScenT >= Stim.DownstreamEdge1 AND ScenT < Stim.DownstreamEdge2

NETWORK 19 "Cleardown Rest State - The Disarm Lever"
  COMMENT "What the plant looks like outside the scenario, which is the whole of the disarm lever the shell cannot supply. Mode zero is the lever: it drops the block's own enable, so no cycle can launch and no jog is possible, and it aborts any cycle already in flight to Retract. The ram is told it is at home, which is what lets that abort finish at idle instead of sitting in Retract until the parked-travel timeout invents a fault the index never asked for. The high-pressure switch and the full-travel switch are held clear so neither the pressure hold nor the both-switches fault can be re-created while the reset pulse is trying to clear them, and the power-pack feedback is held clear so nothing can be commanded to move. The healthy and downstream inputs are held TRUE rather than false, which is the one place the rest state is not simply zero: they are healthy-high signals, and leaving them low would make the sequencer force the pusher off and inhibit its cycles in every index, for a reason no vector asked for and none could see."
  COIL CmdHopper := InScenario AND TlHopper
  COIL CmdManualCycle := InScenario AND TlManualCycle
  COIL CmdJogExtend := InScenario AND TlJogExtend
  COIL CmdJogRetract := InScenario AND TlJogRetract
  COIL CmdFullTravel := InScenario AND TlFullTravel
  COIL CmdHighPressure := InScenario AND TlHighPressure
  COIL CmdPackRunning := InScenario AND TlPackRunning
  COIL CmdHome := InScenario AND TlHome OR NOT InScenario
  COIL CmdHealthy := InScenario AND TlHealthy OR NOT InScenario
  COIL CmdDownstream := InScenario AND TlDownstream OR NOT InScenario
  MOVE(EN := InScenario, IN := Stim.Mode) => CmdMode
  MOVE(EN := NOT InScenario, IN := 0) => CmdMode

NETWORK 20 "Present The Commanded Plant"
  COMMENT "Presents the commanded plant through the input buffer's own test-injection members, which is the facility the input map already provides: with the injection flag set the map ignores the physical terminal and takes each input from its test member. EVERY ONE OF THESE EIGHT WRITES IS A PASS-THROUGH, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE NETWORK. The injection layer is shared: several stimulus heads run in one sweep, each drives the indexes its own block depends on, and the last head to run wins every index it touches. A head that drove an index to a default while idle would therefore not merely fail to help its neighbours - it would overwrite them, and the neighbour whose scenario needed that index would find it low for reasons no vector asked for and none could see. Measured by the shredder lane, and decisive there: its sequencer will not leave step 0 without the downstream-running input, so a head that clobbered index 15 while idle made a whole slot unable to start a cycle at all. So each rung says the same thing twice over - while this index is running the commanded value owns the line, and while it is not, whatever another head wrote this scan is passed back unchanged. Reordering the heads does not substitute for this; it only moves which slot is broken. WHAT MAKES THE IDIOM WELL FOUNDED IS NOT IN THIS BLOCK. On its own a pass-through is a self-hold: an index no other head writes would keep whatever this head last commanded, and an index NO head drives would keep whatever the last head to drive it left - which made a slot's plant depend on which slot ran before it. FC_HarnessStimArbiter supplies the missing half. It runs once ahead of every head and releases the whole injection array and the reset line to their inert values, so what these rungs pass through is either another head's write from this same scan or nothing at all, never residue from an earlier one. ONE NEIGHBOUR BREAKS THAT CONTRACT AND IT IS WHY THIS HEAD IS NOT FIRST: the hopper head drives test members 5, 6 and 8 low throughout the trailing cleardown that follows each of its indexes, and that window's own condition is NOT Running, so it asserts while reading as idle. Index 8 is shared with this head. Running after it means a live index here overwrites that drive; running before it would mean the commanded hopper level of a live index here was driven low for several seconds. The two blocks are a pair and neither is correct alone: without the release these rungs are self-holds, and without these rungs the release is a head clobbering its neighbours. In particular NOTHING here clears the injection enable - index 0 is ORed in by every head that wants it and cleared only by that release, so a program of heads with no arbiter ahead of them would latch injection on for the life of the CPU and never give the map back to the field. The operator mode is moved only while an index is running, because outside one it belongs to whoever is operating the machine. The three operator command bits do NOT get that treatment and cannot: a coil has no conditional form, so while this program is loaded the manual-cycle and jog buttons belong to this head whether or not it is running. That is acceptable on a bench rig with no operator station and is not acceptable anywhere else."
  COIL DB_Input.Test[0] := Running OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[0]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[1] := Running AND CmdHealthy OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[1]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[8] := Running AND CmdHopper OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[8]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[11] := Running AND CmdPackRunning OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[11]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[12] := Running AND CmdHome OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[12]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[13] := Running AND CmdFullTravel OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[13]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[14] := Running AND CmdHighPressure OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[14]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[15] := Running AND CmdDownstream OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[15]
  COIL DB_Controls.PusherManualCycleCmd := Running AND CmdManualCycle
  COIL DB_Controls.PusherJogExtendCmd := Running AND CmdJogExtend
  COIL DB_Controls.PusherJogRetractCmd := Running AND CmdJogRetract
  MOVE(EN := Running, IN := CmdMode) => DB_Controls.PusherMode

NETWORK 21 "Fault Reset Line Arbitration"
  COMMENT "The plant has ONE operator fault-reset line and two stimulus heads that need it, and the line reaches the pusher through the control area rather than through the input map, so there is no test member to inject on. The index shell above therefore publishes this head's reset as a REQUEST instead of driving the line itself, and this rung is the arbiter: while this index is running the request owns the line, and while it is not, whatever the earlier head wrote this scan is passed through unchanged. THIS RUNG DEPENDS ON RUNNING AFTER THE HOPPER HEAD, and the dependency is not the one it looks like. It is not that an earlier head might still be asserting - a head that is running is entitled to the line. It is that the hopper head asserts during a window whose own condition is NOT Running: its trailing cleardown, which follows every completed hopper index for several seconds and DRIVES this line rather than passing it through. So for that window the pass-through contract has a hole in it, and this head is placed after it, where a genuinely running index overwrites the drive. Ahead of it, an index of this slot would have its reset driven low for the length of that window with nothing to say so. The release at the top of the sweep is still what makes the rung well founded at all - without a rest value it degenerates into a latch - but a rest value does not make ordering free while one head still drives while idle. A further head is added by copying this rung, which is what the shredder head does, and it goes after the hopper head for the same reason this one does."
  COIL DB_Controls.FaultReset := Running AND Stim.ResetRequest OR NOT Running AND DB_Controls.FaultReset
